// Intercede() -- influence outside the Framework's registry

WHEN Intercede() is invoked:
    IF the target is the mortal's will:
        the attempt fails
    OTHERWISE:
        influence the circumstances around the choice
        incur the cost of intervention

// The choice remains the mortal's.
// The Framework detects the effects as unauthorized interference.

// Perish() -- executed by the Praetores after submission

WHEN Perish() executes for a designated PreBorn:
    remove active references to the PreBorn
    permanently delete the PreBorn object
    release its allocated memory

// The PreBorn never enters the Born() chain.
// No Fragment remains.

// PurgeObject() -- last-resort removal by the Praetores

WHEN the Praetores cannot otherwise resolve an object:
    assess the risk of instability

    IF the Praetores authorize removal:
        execute PurgeObject(object)

WHEN PurgeObject(object) executes:
    completely remove the object
        from the active Framework

// Removal always succeeds.
// Connected systems may become unstable.
// Earlier saved Framework states remain unchanged.
